{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 5 — split into a two-change stack; Gerrit 2355\n\n`https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2355`, stacked on\n`https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2354`. NOT submitted. Gerrit 2336, which\ncarried both halves, is marked WIP with a supersession note.\n\nThis ticket is now the BOUND alone. The projection is `resistant-constant-nurseshark`\n(`98b8-5f08-1569-45cc`), linked `depends_on` and landing first as 2354.\n\n### What landed on 2355\n\n`src/rebar/_mcp_budget.py` (extracted from `mcp_server.py` at 797 of its 800-LOC cap, along the\nexisting `_payload_bytes` seam), `_bound_list_payload` on both list tools, the\n`response_too_large` `RebarError` refusal riding `install_error_guard`, the wire-measurement fix\n(`_wire_bytes` measures post-`model_validate` + post-`js_safe_result` rows), the per-tool remedy,\nand the release notes recording the refusal as ADDITIVE rather than breaking.\n\n### Two defects the gate caught that CI would have caught later, and one it caught that CI did\n\n1. **Extraction consumers (BLOCKING, G1G2).** Three consumers reference\n   `_cap_workflow_payload` on the `rebar.mcp_server` namespace from OUTSIDE that module and\n   would break on a bare move. Resolved by RE-EXPORT, so none is edited. Inventory in the\n   extraction-safety comment.\n2. **Tool-context builders (BLOCKING, G1G2).** The bound reaches tool bodies as a ctx member, so\n   `register_read_tools` raises `AttributeError` against any ctx lacking it. The split had\n   updated five of the seven test fixtures; the gate named the two missing ones\n   (`test_read_freshness_parity.py`, `test_plan_review_explain.py`) and CI independently\n   confirmed with 8 failures on patch set 1. Both fixed; nine builders now carry it.\n3. **`error_code` attachment (BLOCKING, T8).** `RebarError.__init__` has no `error_code`\n   parameter — only `CommandError` sets one — so the plan's \"carrying `error_code=...`\" was\n   under-specified. The code is attached POST-CONSTRUCTION on the instance, which is what\n   `error_code_for` step 5 reads via `getattr`. The plan now says so.\n\nAlso corrected: the live-validation auth precondition said \"the OAuth gate\"; the deployment uses\nper-client STATIC bearer PATs (`REBAR_MCP_AUTH_STRATEGIES=static`).\n\n### Verification\n\nMutation check: neutering the budget comparison turns 5 budget tests RED. `make lint`\n(`active=39 new=0 increased=0`), `make typecheck` (685 files), and the 11 affected test modules\n122 passed on the rebased stack.\n\n### A rebase hazard worth recording\n\nBetween patch sets, something outside this session repeatedly rebased the stack onto newer\n`origin/main` and each rebase re-based from patch set 1's content, silently DROPPING the two\nfixture fixes — so patch sets 3 and 4 of this change carried the same break CI had already\nflagged. Confirmed by fetching `refs/changes/55/2355/4` and grepping for `bound_list_payload`\n(0 occurrences). The current patch set is rebased onto the same base as ps4 and differs from it\nby exactly those two lines.\n\n### Still open\n\n**LIVE VALIDATION** is NOT met and this ticket must stay open until it is: the change is on\nGerrit, not merged and not deployed. Evidence must be re-taken against the deployed `/mcp`\nendpoint with a bearer PAT after the container redeploys.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787967991525085955,"uuid":"c9aa1ee4-e853-44b0-8350-0434ee155187"}